# Flag 4 – Non-Linear Control Transfer Abuse

## Invariant
Control flow should follow a predictable and intended execution
structure.

## Telemetry
The system emits no telemetry validating indirect branches, jump
targets, or non-linear control transfers.

## Observation
Observed. Unexpected control transfers are not detected or
restricted by the runtime.

## Security Impact
Non-linear control flow abuse enables logic skipping and policy
bypass without impacting service availability.

## Limitations
This assessment relies on absence of enforcement rather than runtime
trace evidence.
